From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:28:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Poll passively for reading tags

Reader/writer mode requested active polling for NFC-A and NFC-F as well.
Tags only answer passive polling; active modes belong to peer-to-peer,
which still adds them. The ST21NFC (NCI 2.0) in the Volla Phone Plinius
rejects RF_DISCOVER_CMD with the active modes (status REJECTED), so no tag
was ever found.
---
 src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c b/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c
index 61484f2..4bab692 100644
--- a/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c
+++ b/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c
@@ -298,9 +298,14 @@ nci_transition_idle_to_discovery_discover(
      */
 
     if (sm->op_mode & NFC_OP_MODE_RW) {
-        techs |= NCI_TECH_A_POLL |
+        /*
+         * Tags only answer passive polling. Active polling is for
+         * peer-to-peer (added below) and some NCI 2.0 controllers
+         * (e.g. ST21NFC) reject RF_DISCOVER_CMD with active modes.
+         */
+        techs |= NCI_TECH_A_POLL_PASSIVE |
             NCI_TECH_B_POLL |
-            NCI_TECH_F_POLL |
+            NCI_TECH_F_POLL_PASSIVE |
             NCI_TECH_V_POLL;
     }
 
